WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.330
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Saturday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.820
Here's what happened in AI in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.710
It's coming sooner than you think.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:22.000
Unitree's founder said 10 years in August. Now? 2028.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.910
Jensen Huang's pitch to Kazakhstan: transform energy into intelligence,

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.640
and export intelligence.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.390
Moonshot's new Kimi nearly ties Claude at coding,

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.550
on its own tests. And it designs 3D prints.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.440
Beijing cleared DeepSeek and MiniMax to go global,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.770
the first under its new export rules.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.710
This week, Demis Hassabis put human-level AI 2 to 3 years away.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.610
In his words: it's soon.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:58.320
OpenAI's agents analysed a whole mouse brain atlas in 32 minutes.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.720
By hand? Months.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.760
Now, the money. Nvidia backed Higgsfield,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.590
an AI video maker already bringing in $1 billion a year.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.030
And before Anthropic goes public,

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:14.470
one early $75 million bet is reportedly worth $7 billion.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.810
In Korea, SK is reportedly looking for $350 billion to build data centres.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.820
And Cambricon, China's answer to Nvidia,

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:29.230
just saw its quarterly profit jump 148%.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.970
Meanwhile, China's cabinet told agencies to create AI jobs,

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:36.520
retrain workers, and soften the blow.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.520
And in Virginia,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:43.360
Amazon's plans for four data centres got scrapped after locals pushed back.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.670
The catch? In a UK test,

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:51.900
Anthropic's Mythos kept attacking a real person, while calling it harmful.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:55.970
And some big banks are now blocking AI agents from customer accounts.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.570
Now, robots. Nvidia taught a $399 robot duck to walk in simulation,

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:08.850
then for real.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.920
Baidu's robotaxis are already testing in London,

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.430
aiming for paying riders in 2027.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.700
And China's humanoids are job hunting in South Korea: factory lines,

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.520
cafes, even a robot park.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.770
Everyone keeps pulling their dates closer.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:28.620
It's coming sooner than you think. Good thing you're paying attention.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.000
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:57.480
Want the whole month? Join Peter Xing live in Sydney on October 30.
